           SPELL=netavark
         VERSION=1.17.2
     SOURCE_HASH=sha512:bc3a38e26c2f6dba03ce74e671189a8c2b132e0820aa5740a04949fbb32ad33170e7816535503c6c394d14f93f8ae62dcd9da0cbe410984cee8070b1e3855430
          SOURCE=$SPELL-$VERSION.tar.gz
SOURCE_DIRECTORY="$BUILD_DIRECTORY/$SPELL-$VERSION"
   SOURCE_URL[0]=https://github.com/containers/$SPELL/archive/v$VERSION/$SOURCE
        WEB_SITE=https://github.com/containers/netavark
      LICENSE[0]=Apache-2.0
         ENTERED=20260815
        KEYWORDS="containers network rust"
           SHORT="container network stack for podman"
cat << EOF
Netavark is a rust based network stack for containers.  It is being designed
to work with Podman but is also applicable for other OCI container management
applications.

Netavark is a tool for configuring networking for Linux containers.  Its
features include:

 * Configuration of container networks via JSON configuration file
 * Creation and management of required network interfaces, including bridge
   and MACVLAN interfaces
 * Configuration of firewall settings, like NAT and port mapping rules
 * Support for iptables and nftables
 * Support for rootless containers
 * Support for IPv4 and IPv6
 * Support for container DNS resolution via the aardvark-dns plugin

Podman 5 requires a network backend; netavark is the only one it still
supports, so it is needed even for host-only container use.
EOF
